      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Ya contamos cómo Ra mandó su Ojo contra los humanos, y el Ojo se volvió Sekhmet.",
          "en": "We already told how Ra sent his Eye against humans, and the Eye became Sekhmet."
        },
        {
          "es": "En otro cuento, mucho más tardío, el Ojo se enojó con Ra y huyó al sur, a Nubia.",
          "en": "In another, much later tale, the Eye got angry with Ra and fled south, to Nubia."
        },
        {
          "es": "Sin su Ojo, Ra se debilitó y Egipto sufrió. Ra mandó a Thoth y a Shu a buscarla.",
          "en": "Without his Eye, Ra grew weak and Egypt suffered. Ra sent Thoth and Shu to find her."
        },
        {
          "es": "Thoth le contó fábulas para calmarla. Ella volvió a Egipto con música, danza y vino.",
          "en": "Thoth told her fables to calm her. She returned to Egypt with music, dance, and wine."
        },
        {
          "es": "Al volver, la leona furiosa se tranquilizó y se volvió la dulce Hathor.",
          "en": "Once home, the furious lioness grew calm and became gentle Hathor."
        }
      ],
